@startuml
' =============================================================================
' Amazon Bedrock batch inference — statuses of a model invocation job — UML state diagram
'
' Mermaid source set : none (no numbered set covers batch inference); this view is
'                      drawn from the chapter 01-amazon-bedrock/inference/08-batch-inference.md
'                      ("Job states" table and its job-lifecycle sequence diagram) and
'                      complements diagram set 03 (model inference lifecycle).
' Verified           : 2026-11-15
' Status             : academy design, not an official AWS reference architecture.
'                      Only the ten documented status values are drawn. The API reference
'                      describes each status but publishes no transition table: solid
'                      transitions follow a status description directly, dashed ones are
'                      our reading. No AWS icons; nothing is included from the network.
'
' Official sources this view relies on:
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_GetModelInvocationJob.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/APIReference/API_CreateModelInvocationJob.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/batch-inference-monitor.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/batch-inference-stop.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/capacity-limits-cost-optimization.html
'   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/monitoring-eventbridge.html
'
' What UML adds: which statuses are final, and which events move a job between them.
' =============================================================================
!pragma layout smetana
title Amazon Bedrock batch inference — statuses of a model invocation job (UML state)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam stateBorderColor #555555
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #888888
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam legendBorderColor #888888

state "Not final — StopModelInvocationJob is accepted" as active #FFFBF5;line:D97706 {
  state "Submitted" as Submitted #E8F1FB;line:1F6FEB : queued for validation
  state "Validating" as Validating #E8F1FB;line:1F6FEB : role access to Amazon S3,\n.jsonl record format,\nfile-size and record quotas
  state "Scheduled" as Scheduled #E6F4EA;line:1E8E3E : validated; waiting in a queue;\non-demand traffic takes priority
  state "InProgress" as InProgress #E6F4EA;line:1E8E3E : results start to appear\nin the output S3 location
}

state "Stopping" as Stopping #FDECEA;line:C62828 : being stopped by a user
state "Completed" as Completed #E6F4EA;line:1E8E3E : final · check errorRecordCount
state "PartiallyCompleted" as PartiallyCompleted #FFF8E1;line:B28704 : final · not all records\nprocessed in time
state "Expired" as Expired #FFF8E1;line:B28704 : final · did not begin before\nthe timeout · submit a new job
state "Failed" as Failed #FDECEA;line:C62828 : final · see the message field
state "Stopped" as Stopped #FDECEA;line:C62828 : final · tokens already\nprocessed are charged

[*] --> Submitted : CreateModelInvocationJob\nreturns jobArn at once
Submitted --> Validating
Validating --> Scheduled : validation passed
Validating -[dashed]-> Failed : validation failed\n(role or S3 permission, format)
Scheduled --> InProgress : reaches its turn
Scheduled --> Expired : timeoutDurationInHours elapsed\n(24 to 168; default 24)
InProgress --> Completed : all records processed
InProgress --> PartiallyCompleted : not all records\nprocessed in time
InProgress -[dashed]-> Failed
active -[dashed]-> Stopping : StopModelInvocationJob
Stopping --> Stopped

Completed --> [*]
PartiallyCompleted --> [*]
Expired --> [*]
Failed --> [*]
Stopped --> [*]

note right of InProgress
  A bad record does not fail the job: it gets an error
  object in the output. Progress = processedRecordCount
  / totalRecordCount (can lag by up to 1 minute)
end note

note bottom of Completed
  Each status change can reach Amazon EventBridge as
  "Batch Inference Job State Change" (source aws.bedrock,
  best-effort delivery). Re-read the job with
  GetModelInvocationJob before acting on an event
  (academy recommendation)
end note

legend right
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | solid transition | follows directly from the documented status description |
  | dashed transition | our reading — not stated as a transition by AWS |
  | composite state | any status inside it can be stopped (our reading) |
  |<#E8F1FB> blue | accepted, not yet validated |
  |<#E6F4EA> green | running or finished normally |
  |<#FFF8E1> yellow | final, some or all records not processed |
  |<#FDECEA> red | failed or stopped |
  Statuses: Submitted · Validating · Scheduled · InProgress · Completed · PartiallyCompleted ·
  Failed · Stopping · Stopped · Expired (GetModelInvocationJob, status field)
  Academy design · not an official AWS diagram · Verified 2026-11-15
endlegend
@enduml
